// Typed handles and tables: AST nodes, types, fns, modules and IR values live in per-stage `Pool<T>`s
// addressed by `Id<T>`, so an `Id<Expr>` never mixes with an `Id<Stmt>`; spans live on the side.
//
// Port of: j3c/src/ir/ids.rs
// J3: `Pool<T>` / `Id<T>` are `j3.data.pool`; this adds `Spans<T>`, a side table `Id<T>` to `Span` (plan 11
// B4). Nodes carry no span inline: cheap equality and hashing, stage outputs that can be cached (B5),
// read-only tables shared across threads. Lives in base because AST, typed tree, IR and UI trees all use it.
module j3c.base.ids;
